Alternatively, the characteristic polynomial of $A$ can also be expressed in terms of the sums of its principal minors as
\begin{equation}\label{eqn:C-H-Thm-f-as coef}
p_A(\lambda) = \lambda^n - f_1 \lambda^{n-1} + f_2 \lambda^{n-2} - \cdots + (-1)^{n-k} f_{n-k} \lambda^{k} + \cdots + (-1)^n f_n,
\end{equation}
where $f_i$ denotes the sum of all principal minors of order $i$ of $A$. 
Comparing Equations~\eqref{Eqn:c-h-thm,coeef-as-d} and~\eqref{eqn:C-H-Thm-f-as coef}, we obtain
\[
d_i = (-1)^i f_i, \qquad \text{for each } i \in [n].
\]
Since $f_i$ is the sum of all principal minors of order $i$, it can equivalently be expressed as a weighted sum over linear subdigraphs of $\mathcal{D}(A)$:
\begin{equation}\label{Eqn:fi=sum lsd}
f_i = \sum_{\gamma} (-1)^{i - c(\gamma)} \, w(\gamma),
\end{equation}
where the summation extends over all linear subdigraphs $\gamma$ of $\mathcal{D}(A)$ containing $i$ vertices.

