The following sections present the range of models employed in this study. In each case, the survival function forms are specified according to a single particular rate-shape distributional family such that $X \sim Family (\alpha, \lambda)$ and $Y \sim Family (\beta(0), \nu)$ where $\alpha$ and $\beta(0)$ denote the rate parameters and $\lambda$ and $\nu$ denote the shape parameters (shape parameters are not applicable for exponential and half-Cauchy models, however). Closed-form expressions of the models' moments are derived, and additionally, theoretical correlation bounds are obtained (with the exception of the half-Cauchy and gamma models).

