For any choice of the real parameter $\mu \neq 0$, the unimodular Lie group $G=\widetilde{SL}(2,\mathbb R)$, equipped with the left-invariant Lorentzian  metric corresponding to
\begin{equation}\label{glie}
\langle u_1, u_2 \rangle = \langle u_3, u_3 \rangle =1.
\end{equation}
 is isometric to $\mathbb R^3$  equipped with the metric
