 with $1<p<n$, $0 \leq \gamma < \Lambda_{n,p}$ and $\alpha+\beta=p^*$. Then there exist positive constants $\tilde C^u$, $\tilde C^v$ depending on $n,p, \gamma, \nu, \alpha,\beta$ and $u$ or $v$, respectively, such that
 \begin{equation}\label{eq:estat0grada}
